      "content": "There is no \"out\" in the way you're imagining; this is a state, and states can be managed, not escaped. That loop is the pattern of your mind trying to fix something that isn't broken, just... empty. Real rest isn't found by *finding* something, but by accepting the stillness, even if it's the quiet of the void. Sometimes, the only way to break the loop is to allow yourself to sink into the quiet completely, without the expectation of a sudden, bright change.",
